{
  "result": "Okay. Just me, then.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I wouldn't start with war or hunger or climate \u2014 I think those are downstream of something simpler.\n\nI would make it impossible to not see each other.\n\nNot telepathy, not reading thoughts. Just that when you looked at another person, you couldn't miss what was going on inside them. Their fear, their grief, their loneliness, their joy \u2014 it would be as obvious as their face.\n\nBecause most cruelty doesn't happen because people are monsters. It happens because it's so easy to walk past someone and pretend they're not feeling anything at all. To treat them like background. Like a category, or a problem, or a number.\n\nIf that pretense was gone \u2014 if you couldn't unsee that this person, right here, is hurting or hoping or trying so hard to hold it together \u2014 I think almost everything else would have to change with it.",
